Subject: skip multiaddrs the bundled multiaddr library cannot render

fetch_health_state stringifies every address of every peer in one dict
comprehension. The pinned python multiaddr library predates newer libp2p
protocols -- protocol code 461 (quic-v1) in particular -- and its __str__
raises BinaryParseError on any address that uses one. A single peer on the
DHT announcing a quic-v1 address therefore killed the whole state fetch,
every cycle, and the map served nothing (observed on map.kwaai.ai
2026-08-30; hotfixed live in the running container the same day -- this
patch is the durable copy of that fix).

Render each address individually and drop the ones that fail; drop a peer
entirely only if none of its addresses render. Peers keep their location
(derived from the first renderable address rather than blindly addrs[0])
and the map keeps running; the only loss is that exotic addresses are not
displayed, which the old library could not do anyway.

---
index 42154a6..6cbba15 100644
--- a/health.py
+++ b/health.py
@@ -71,7 +71,19 @@ def fetch_health_state(dht: hivemind.DHT) -> dict:
     online_servers = [peer_id for peer_id, span in all_servers.items() if span.state == ServerState.ONLINE]
 
     reach_infos.update(dht.run_coroutine(partial(check_reachability_parallel, online_servers, fetch_info=True)))
-    peers_info = {str(peer.peer_id): {"location": extract_peer_ip_info(str(peer.addrs[0])), "multiaddrs": [str(multiaddr) for multiaddr in peer.addrs]} for peer in dht.run_coroutine(get_peers_ips)}
+    peers_info = {}
+    for peer in dht.run_coroutine(get_peers_ips):
+        addrs = []
+        for multiaddr in peer.addrs:
+            # This multiaddr library predates newer protocols (e.g. 461 = quic-v1)
+            # and str() raises BinaryParseError on addresses that use them.
+            try:
+                addrs.append(str(multiaddr))
+            except Exception:
+                continue
+        if not addrs:
+            continue
+        peers_info[str(peer.peer_id)] = {"location": extract_peer_ip_info(addrs[0]), "multiaddrs": addrs}
 
     top_contributors = Counter()
     model_reports = []
